{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104853","id":2429522501,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Qz5JF","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104853","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104853.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104853.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104853","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104853/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104853/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104853/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/daf8eee9cb7726ff02d9dafee52dce061131d799","number":104853,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix AudioStreamPlayer3D stereo panning issue","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103989\r\nIncorporates: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103856\r\nSupersedes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103926\r\n\r\nThis is implemented as suggested in the issue by separating out the `SPEAKER_MODE_STEREO` as a special case and calling `_calc_output_vol_stereo()` instead of `_calc_output_vol()`.  \r\n\r\nObviously the handling of the stereo case in `_calc_output_vol()` is now redundant.  However, I don't think it is wise to touch I cannot test.  Either I've got to get access to a 7.1 speaker arrangement, or use https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103655 or find some other viable method to fake the existence of high numbers of speakers on my development system.\r\n\r\nAlso the I believe documentation is the wrong way round regarding panning_strength on speakers vs headphones.  It's okay to set the panning strength to 1.0 with speakers since you can hear both speakers with both ears.  However it can be unpleasant for headphones to have one side entirely muted.  \r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":572781997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1NzI3ODE5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:audio","name":"topic:audio","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8089024095,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAAB4iS2Xw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/cherrypick:4.4","name":"cherrypick:4.4","description":"Considered for cherry-picking into a future 4.4.x release","color":"4466